  "answer_text": "The **comic book** came first! Here's a quick breakdown:\n\n- **The Comic:** *The Walking Dead* is an American post-apocalyptic comic book series created by writer Robert Kirkman and artist Tony Moore. Beginning in **2003** and published by Image Comics, the series ran for 193 issues, with Kirkman unexpectedly ending the series in 2019.\n\n- **The TV Show:** In January 2010, AMC ordered a pilot for *The Walking Dead*, based on the comic book of the same name and developed by Frank Darabont and Gale Anne Hurd. Andrew Lincoln was cast as Rick Grimes, and the show premiered on **October 31, 2010**.\n\nSo the comic predates the TV show by about **7 years**. The AMC television series loosely follows the storyline of the comic book.",
